-- `Refines` defines adjective-refined commands on existing types and
-- spec-infix relations, including `implicitly:`/`explicitly:` markers and
-- composite `[[subject]]` refinements.


-- Nonempty sets: at least one element belongs to `X`.
[\(nonempty)::set]
Refines: X
satisfies:
. exists: x is \element:of{X}
  suchThat: x "in"? X
Appendix:
. adjective: "nonempty"
Id: "dff130c9-4fc4-4bd5-a7b0-dd6ee7a1ff23"


-- Commutative magmas: the binary operation satisfies `a * b = b * a`.
[\(commutative)::magma]
Refines: M ::= (X, *)
satisfies:
. forAll: a, b "in" X
  then: a * b = b * a
Appendix:
. adjective: "commutative"
Id: "b6c0c765-d12c-437c-80e1-7a0113e8b789"


-- `implicitly:` declares that this subtype refinement merely restates the
-- inherited refinement on `\set`.
[\(nonempty)::magma]
Refines: M ::= (X, *)
implicitly:
specifies: M is \(nonempty)::set
Appendix:
. adjective: "nonempty"
Id: "9411125d-e05c-41ff-9b1e-fc55f9547604"


-- `explicitly:` declares that this subtype refinement adds a concrete property
-- beyond the inherited `specifies:` fact (here that the identity witnesses
-- nonemptiness).
[\(nonempty)::monoid]
Refines: M ::= (X, *, e)
explicitly:
specifies: M is \(nonempty)::magma
satisfies: e "in"? X
Appendix:
. adjective: "nonempty"
Id: "aeda535b-696d-426a-916c-da930f1d5d94"


-- Injective, surjective, and bijective functions, demonstrating composite
-- refinement with `[[f]]` in `specifies:`.
[\(injective)::function:on{A}:to{B}]
Refines: f(x__)
when: A, B is \set
satisfies:
. forAll: x, y "in" A
  where: f(x) = f(y)
  then: x = y
Appendix:
. adjective: "injective"
Id: "f1a2b3c4-4444-4aaa-8bbb-000000000001"


[\(surjective)::function:on{A}:to{B}]
Refines: f(x__)
when: A, B is \set
satisfies:
. forAll: y "in" B
  then:
  . exists: x "in" A
    suchThat: f(x) = y
Appendix:
. adjective: "surjective"
Id: "f1a2b3c4-4444-4aaa-8bbb-000000000002"


[\(bijective)::function:on{A}:to{B}]
Refines: f(x__)
when: A, B is \set
specifies: f is \(injective, surjective)::[[f]]
Appendix:
. adjective: "bijective"
Id: "f1a2b3c4-4444-4aaa-8bbb-000000000003"


-- A refined spec-infix command: a proper subset omits at least one element of
-- the ambient set `B`.
[A \:(proper)::subset:/ B]
Refines: A
when: B is \set
satisfies:
. exists: b "in" B
  suchThat: \\not{b "in"? A}
Appendix:
. adjective: "proper"
. written: "A? \subsetneq B?"
Id: "9d1238e3-30db-4e78-a3ac-e53ccf6dd887"


-- A refinement of a base type propagates through its subtype chain, and a
-- composite refinement implies each individual adjective.
Theorem:
given:
. G ::= (X, *, e) is \group
. A, B is \set
. f is \(bijective)::function:on{A}:to{B}
where: G is \(nonempty)::monoid
then:
. G is? \(nonempty)::magma
. G is? \(nonempty)::set
. f is? \(injective)::function:on{A}:to{B}
. f is? \(surjective)::function:on{A}:to{B}
Appendix:
. called: "refinements follow subtype chains and composite adjectives"
Id: "7474854b-5143-4d83-a0bb-50e943ace450"
